with a noose tied around his neck.

00:11:28.610 --> 00:11:31.318
Some people in the crowd were convinced that Burroughs was innocent and that

00:11:31.324 --> 00:11:32.390
his life should be spared.

00:11:32.470 --> 00:11:35.430
Cotton Mather called it an anomaly and hung him anyways.

00:11:35.510 --> 00:11:36.214
Back to Caleb.

00:11:36.262 --> 00:11:38.986
The family begins to recite the Lord's Prayer and to the surprise of

00:11:39.008 --> 00:11:42.458
everyone except for Thomasin, only the twins seem unable to recite the prayer.

00:11:42.464 --> 00:11:45.598
They claim that they've forgotten it and that it's making them ill.

00:11:45.684 --> 00:11:48.682
This is pretty solid evidence that the twins are possessed but Katherine

00:11:48.746 --> 00:11:51.002
doesn't want to believe this, so all hell breaks loose.

00:11:51.066 --> 00:11:54.206
Caleb interrupts the chaos again, claiming that The Witch is back.

00:11:54.308 --> 00:11:55.360
Roll it.

00:11:58.210 --> 00:11:59.434
No, not that clip.

00:11:59.482 --> 00:11:59.892
Come on.

00:11:59.892 --> 00:12:00.750
This clip

00:12:02.155 --> 00:12:09.942
-[Caleb] A toad. A cat. A crow. A raven. 

00:12:10.890 --> 00:12:13.788
-[Caleb] A great black dog. A wolf. 

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:16.950
-[Caleb] She desires my blood. She sends 'em upon me.

00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:23.146
This could be interpreted as the real Caleb trying to communicate with his

00:12:23.168 --> 00:12:26.326
family about The Witch's ability to manipulate animals and this knowledge

00:12:26.358 --> 00:12:28.682
could prevent them from being accusatory towards each other.

00:12:28.736 --> 00:12:31.686
The family prays around Caleb and Caleb prays for himself.

00:12:31.798 --> 00:12:35.214
This culminates in a last resort prayer that he screams out and it almost

00:12:35.252 --> 00:12:37.486
resembles the peak of an adult act.

00:12:37.588 --> 00:12:40.042
If you look at the script, it also makes this comparison.

00:12:40.106 --> 00:12:43.338
This is fitting because The Witch initially drew him in by taking advantage

00:12:43.354 --> 00:12:45.590
of the prepubescent boy's blossoming lust.

00:12:45.690 --> 00:12:49.038
During this prayer, he accepts the Lord's salvation and dies. Die!

00:12:49.134 --> 00:12:51.342
Due to her existing suspicions.

00:12:51.406 --> 00:12:54.866
Katherine screams at Thomasin unable to see past the idea that she is a witch.

00:12:54.888 --> 00:12:58.022
This is probably a good time to add a little more context around

00:12:58.076 --> 00:13:01.826
Puritans and how their specific hysterical brand of faith blurred the lines

00:13:01.858 --> 00:13:05.526
between folklore and reality eventually leading to paranoia, hysteria and

00:13:05.548 --> 00:13:06.710
the death of innocent people.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:10.054
The Puritans left Europe not because they were persecuted but because they

00:13:10.092 --> 00:13:12.082
thought that they were too pure to live in Europe.

00:13:12.146 --> 00:13:15.162
If anything, they felt persecuted because they were surrounded by people

00:13:15.216 --> 00:13:16.810
that weren't as holy as they were.

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:19.610
When they came to New England, they brought that same attitude with them.

00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:22.346
They felt that the new frontier in the wilderness surrounding them was

00:13:22.368 --> 00:13:24.330
untouched by people as faithful as them.

00:13:24.400 --> 00:13:27.914
It was a land where the devil and evil thrived and the proof of their theory

00:13:27.962 --> 00:13:29.502
was that it was very hard to live there.

00:13:29.556 --> 00:13:30.782
They weren't suited for it.

00:13:30.836 --> 00:13:34.446
When it was too cold to go outside, grow crops or even go to church it was

00:13:34.468 --> 00:13:37.558
because the devil was testing them not because they'd made a stupid choice,

00:13:37.594 --> 00:13:40.786
By moving to a cold, unfamiliar wilderness. They felt that they were

00:13:40.808 --> 00:13:43.698
constantly being tried and tested which we see at the beginning of the movie

00:13:43.704 --> 00:13:46.786
in William and Caleb's dialogue, they repeatedly stepped on

00:13:46.808 --> 00:13:49.950
metaphorical rakes and blamed Satan when the handle hit their heads.

00:13:50.030 --> 00:13:52.898
The family at the center of this movie considered themselves to be too pure

00:13:52.914 --> 00:13:55.698
for the Puritan plantation that they had been living on in England.

00:13:55.794 --> 00:13:58.886
The very first scene of the movie shows them excommunicating themselves from

00:13:58.908 --> 00:13:59.878
their original home.

00:13:59.964 --> 00:14:02.906
This is relevant to my analysis of The Witch because her actions in

00:14:02.928 --> 00:14:05.194
manipulation have shaken the faith of this family.

00:14:05.312 --> 00:14:08.666
Katherine is distraught and feels that she may never experience the love she

00:14:08.688 --> 00:14:10.150
knew before Samuel died.

00:14:10.230 --> 00:14:12.742
William and Katherine suspect that Thomasin is a witch.

00:14:12.806 --> 00:14:15.966
Thomasin strongly suspects that the twins are possessed by the devil, not

00:14:15.988 --> 00:14:18.974
to mention two of the family's five children are dead, which would be enough

00:14:19.012 --> 00:14:21.882
to test the faith of even the most pure of puritans.

00:14:22.026 --> 00:14:25.358
Not knowing what else to do, William barricades the twins and Thomasin in

00:14:25.364 --> 00:14:27.302
the barn with Black Phillip and the other goats.

00:14:27.386 --> 00:14:30.750
Katherine decides to sleep outside in the grave that they've dug for Caleb,

00:14:30.830 --> 00:14:33.342
which I guess is one way to deal with mourning.

00:14:33.406 --> 00:14:35.582
I think that this represents her emotional death.

00:14:35.646 --> 00:14:38.738
After losing her two kids, she no longer feels like she can love again.

00:14:38.824 --> 00:14:41.346
William chops wood and confesses for his sins.

00:14:41.458 --> 00:14:44.466
This is how their last night as a family begins, and how their puritan

00:14:44.498 --> 00:14:47.506
nightmare finally ends, and The Witch that has been haunting them would

00:14:47.548 --> 00:14:50.570
bring the full force of her evil magic to tear them apart.

00:14:50.757 --> 00:14:53.256
(Impact)

00:14:55.666 --> 00:14:58.937
♪ Mysterious Music ♪

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:02.826
Who knows what happened to Katherine as she slept out in the grave, but when

00:15:02.848 --> 00:15:05.290
we next see her, she's entering the house through a window.

00:15:05.370 --> 00:15:09.150
She sees Caleb holding baby Samuel in his arms, both alive and well.

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:12.334
She hugs him, and he whispers to her in a voice that some might find alarm.

00:15:12.372 --> 00:15:16.222
-[Caleb] Mother. We have longed to see you so. 

00:15:16.356 --> 00:15:18.738
Caleb has a book that he wants his mother to sign.

00:15:18.824 --> 00:15:21.954
Katherine is receptive to the idea, but first notices that Samuel seems hungry.

00:15:21.992 --> 00:15:24.898
and when she goes to breastfeed him, she seems not to notice that

00:15:24.904 --> 00:15:27.870
she's actually holding a raven who pecks at her bloody breast.

00:15:27.950 --> 00:15:30.418
Another example of The Witch's manipulation of animals.

00:15:30.514 --> 00:15:34.594
When a witch takes the form of a raven dog, rabbit, or most famously, cats,

00:15:34.642 --> 00:15:36.770
these animals are known as The Witch's familiar.

00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:39.926
The Witch would transform into these animals and provide them sustenance by

00:15:39.948 --> 00:15:42.146
feeding them with the blood that flowed from her nipples.

00:15:42.258 --> 00:15:43.894
This explains the previous scene.

00:15:43.942 --> 00:15:45.974
Witches were also thought to have an extra nipple.

00:15:46.022 --> 00:15:48.870
This is where the phrase a witch's tit comes from, apparently.

00:15:48.950 --> 00:15:51.946
Back in the barn, the twins wake up to the sound of heavy breathing and

00:15:51.968 --> 00:15:55.198
footsteps to see The Witch in her true form sucking the blood from one of

00:15:55.204 --> 00:15:55.786
the goats.

00:15:55.898 --> 00:15:58.942
She turns and tackles at the children, who see her face for the first time,

00:15:58.996 --> 00:16:02.174
drawing screams from Thomasin. During the night, The Witch possessed

00:16:02.212 --> 00:16:04.522
Black Phillip to tear apart the barn and kill the twins.

00:16:04.586 --> 00:16:07.934
Or at least we can assume that's why William wakes up and discovers his barn destroyed. 

00:16:07.982 --> 00:16:11.054
The script includes a detail about Phillip bucking at the barn

00:16:11.102 --> 00:16:14.082
walls that morning, which further confirms that this is probably what took place. 

00:16:14.136 --> 00:16:18.066
He barely has a moment to register before old Black Phillip gores him

00:16:18.088 --> 00:16:19.490
in the stomach with his horns.

00:16:19.570 --> 00:16:23.254
You may be wondering, why has William been spared up until this point?

00:16:23.292 --> 00:16:26.086
Well, we can't answer that, definitely, but one reason why women were

00:16:26.108 --> 00:16:28.918
disproportionately accused of witchcraft was because they were believed to

00:16:28.924 --> 00:16:32.666
be weaker, both physically and in their faith than men, and that has been

00:16:32.688 --> 00:16:33.658
true throughout this story.

00:16:33.744 --> 00:16:35.770
William has an unwavering faith in God.

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:39.094
Thomasin has remained faithful too, despite her family's doubts.

00:16:39.222 --> 00:16:42.362
This could be why Black Phillip and The Witch went for the rest of the family first.

00:16:42.416 --> 00:16:45.706
And this could also explain why William is killed through physical

00:16:45.738 --> 00:16:48.046
force rather than trying to get him to sign the book.

00:16:48.148 --> 00:16:51.950
Katherine comes outside and sees the aftermath of all of this, and yet again

00:16:52.020 --> 00:16:55.246
blames Thomasin, assuming that she must be The Witch because she's the only

00:16:55.268 --> 00:16:57.722
one left standing and her hands are stained with blood.

00:16:57.786 --> 00:17:00.782
This time, Katherine takes action and physically attacks Thomasin.

00:17:00.846 --> 00:17:03.378
Although this is not spelled out in the movie, the fact that she fed the

00:17:03.384 --> 00:17:06.370
raven with her breast would imply that she is now bewitched as well.

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:08.706
Either way, Thomasin reluctantly fights back.

00:17:08.808 --> 00:17:11.446
Only when it's clear that her mother is trying to strangle her does she

00:17:11.468 --> 00:17:13.958
strike back with a rusty bill hook, killing her.

00:17:14.044 --> 00:17:17.558
Now, without any family remaining, Thomasin finds herself alone in the wilderness.

00:17:17.564 --> 00:17:20.726
After seeing what became of the twins, it's fair to say that her

00:17:20.748 --> 00:17:23.802
own faith is starting to waver, and she decides to try speaking to Black Phillip.

00:17:23.856 --> 00:17:27.434
After removing her bloody dress, she goes to the barn and asks

00:17:27.472 --> 00:17:29.590
Black Phillip to speak to her like he did to the twins.

00:17:29.670 --> 00:17:37.626
After a long moment of silence, he responds
-[Black Phillip] What DOST thou want?

00:17:37.658 --> 00:17:40.958
He offers her the chance at a decadent lifestyle and the opportunity to see the world.

00:17:41.044 --> 00:17:43.966
We had previously seen her reminiscing about her time in England, so it

00:17:43.988 --> 00:17:46.018
makes sense that she'd be enticed by this opportunity.

00:17:46.184 --> 00:17:47.986
Of course, it comes at a cost.

00:17:48.088 --> 00:17:50.114
He's got a book for her to sign as well.

00:17:50.232 --> 00:17:56.302
-[Black Phillip]DOST thou see a book before thee? 

00:17:56.366 --> 00:17:59.446
Thomasin removes her clothes, presumably signs the book of the Devil, and follows Black Phillip into the woods,

00:17:59.468 --> 00:18:02.930
where she discovers a bunch of women chanting around a fire with Black Phillip.

00:18:03.010 --> 00:18:06.406
They all levitate into the air, and Thomasin, who has just abandoned her

00:18:06.428 --> 00:18:09.442
faith and modesty joins them, and a new witch is born.

00:18:09.506 --> 00:18:12.454
It's fitting that the history of The Witch is actually the history of two witches.

00:18:12.492 --> 00:18:15.866
The whole purpose of a witch is to cause devastation and to get

00:18:15.888 --> 00:18:18.198
more people to turn away from God to Satan.

00:18:18.294 --> 00:18:21.334
This is what happens to Thomasin, and she only succumbs after The Witch

00:18:21.382 --> 00:18:22.538
takes everything from her.

00:18:22.624 --> 00:18:25.726
It's fitting that the chaos that followed her sister accusing her of being a

00:18:25.748 --> 00:18:28.318
witch is what actually drove her to become one in the end.

00:18:28.404 --> 00:18:31.838
People told stories about witches, and the Puritans were so paranoid and

00:18:31.844 --> 00:18:35.018
forlorn in their new worlds that they turned their fears into actual death

00:18:35.034 --> 00:18:37.130
and destruction in the late 1600s.

00:18:37.210 --> 00:18:40.986
But The VVitch just scratches the surface of the horrifying occult rituals

00:18:41.018 --> 00:18:42.234
in A24 films.

00:18:42.282 --> 00:18:45.478
To get the full picture, you need to check out my analysis of King Paimon

00:18:45.484 --> 00:18:47.526
From Hereditary, which you can find on the left.

00:18:47.628 --> 00:18:51.350
Your homework is to subscribe to CZsWorld for new horrors every week.

00:18:51.420 --> 00:18:55.494
Ring the Death Bell for all notifications and I'll see you in the next video.

00:18:55.612 --> 00:18:57.330
Assuming we both survive.

